<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on Dec 9.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on Dec 9.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonnes tel quel):</p>
<p>Vessel		Position	  Quantity	 Destination</p>
<p>Orient ExpressI   ETD Dec 10	 1,200 (W)	Cambodia</p>
<p>Orient ExpressI   ETA Dec 19-22    1,200 (W)	Cambodia</p>
<p>Pakarti Sembilan  ETA Dec 28	 5,250 (R)	Indonesia</p>
<p>Dien Bien	   ETA Dec 20	 7,000	    Japan</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	 ETR Dec 20	 14,300	    Japan</p>
<p>Pichai Samut	ETA Dec 30	 15,300	    Japan</p>
<p>Ivan Makarin	ETA Dec 28	 17,850	    Japan</p>
<p>Kasuga II	   L/Can Dec 15-22  3,500 (W)	Singapore</p>
<p>NOTE: ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness. L/Can indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled. W means white sugar and R means raw sugar.</p>
</text>
